id: pm-scga6k
title: "GH-855: core mutation locators must honor extension-registered item types"
description: "Active extensions can register custom item type folders that reads and create honor, while core mutation locators omit the active registry. Unify item resolution across close, update, annotations, delete/restore, bulk operations, and workspace transactions, then prove a non-persisted extension type through installed-package lifecycle acceptance."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: "area:extensions","area:sdk",consistency,custom-types,gh-issue,item-lifecycle
created_at: "2026-08-01T13:27:35.279Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-01T14:39:35.613Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-01T14:39:34.889Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-01T14:39:34.889Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "All core item and annotation mutation locators consume the active extension item-type registry; Installed-package end-to-end coverage exercises create, read, update, annotate, close, delete, restore, and bulk or transactional mutation for a non-persisted custom type; Public SDK and CLI behavior stay identical with no private package workaround"
parent: pm-usfg
severity: high
repro_steps: "Install an extension registering Run in runs, create through context.sdk.client, then call client.close or pm update without persisting the type in schema/types.json"
expected_result: Every read and mutation path resolves extension-contributed item folders from the same active registry
actual_result: get/list/create find a registered custom type item while update and close return Item ID not found
affected_version: 2026.8.1
component: sdk/lifecycle/storage
