comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-01T13:27:35.279Z","harness:codex","text=Duplicate check evidence: searched all statuses for GH-855, extension custom type locator, custom folders, mutation lookup, and schema registry. Closed pm-iqq0 and schema lineage provide registration/customization foundations; no item tracks mutation-path registry parity. Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/855"
  "2026-08-01T14:37:35.198Z","harness:codex","Evidence: close lifecycle registry resolution now includes active extension registrations in both duplicate-target lookup and primary target lookup. Installed Run type acceptance covers create, update, comment annotation, atomic transaction update, close, delete, restore, and get from its non-persisted runs folder. Focused linked test passed and the full 6666-test 100/100/100/100 coverage gate passed."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-01T14:37:35.950Z","harness:codex",Every lifecycle locator must resolve the same built-in plus persisted plus active-extension type registry; one core-only close lookup was enough to make a package-defined type appear writable but not closable.
